Pymtheg patch 0011 (C-21, not upstream): attributes on parameters.

Accepts valid Rust: any number of outer attributes on a function parameter
(`#[rustfmt::skip] #[cfg(..)] x: T`; upstream reads only one) and outer
attributes on closure parameters (`|#[allow(unused_variables)] x: bool| ..`).
The attribute items are children of `parameters` / `closure_parameters`
directly before their parameter, as a single attribute already was.
Reference: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/items/functions.html#attributes-on-function-parameters
           https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/closure-expr.html#attributes-on-closure-parameters
Upstream issue: https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust/issues/276
(open, function parameters). No upstream pull request.

diff --git a/grammar.js b/grammar.js
index 36770d8..84b41ee 100644
--- a/grammar.js
+++ b/grammar.js
@@ -674,7 +674,8 @@ module.exports = grammar({
     parameters: $ => seq(
       '(',
       sepBy(',', seq(
-        optional($.attribute_item),
+        // Pymtheg patch 0011 (issue #276): any number of outer attributes.
+        repeat($.attribute_item),
         choice(
           $.parameter,
           $.self_parameter,
@@ -1349,9 +1350,13 @@ module.exports = grammar({
 
     closure_parameters: $ => seq(
       '|',
-      sepBy(',', choice(
-        $._pattern,
-        $.parameter,
+      // Pymtheg patch 0011: closure parameters take outer attributes too.
+      sepBy(',', seq(
+        repeat($.attribute_item),
+        choice(
+          $._pattern,
+          $.parameter,
+        ),
       )),
       '|',
     ),
